  "published": "2026-10-13T11:11:01Z",
  "modified": "2026-10-13T11:11:01Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-63718: mod_proxy_uwsgi: drop hop-by-hop headers from the backend\n  response\n- CVE-2026-73636: mod_auth_digest: accept a one-time nonce only once, also when\n  the client entry was garbage collected\n- CVE-2026-73637: mod_auth_digest: don't use a client entry outside the client\n  lock\n- CVE-2026-48005: mod_auth_digest: track the nonce-count per nonce and record it\n  only for a fully verified request\n- mod_auth_digest: configs using \"AuthDigestQop none\" or the \"authdigest-opaque\"\n  Mutex type no longer start (\"AuthDigestQop none\" in .htaccess: 500; the\n  shipped manual still documents it); RFC 2069 clients (no qop) are refused;\n  with AuthDigestNcCheck On or AuthDigestNonceLifetime 0, 503 if no client\n  entry fits in shared memory; log ids AH01767, AH01771, AH01772, AH01792\n  and AH01793 are removed\n- mod_auth_digest: with AuthDigestNcCheck On, a request that is authenticated\n  twice (e.g. a DirectoryIndex file in its own <Files> section) is refused\n  with 401\n- mod_auth_digest: after a reload (also the logrotate one) or a SIGHUP restart\n  a captured request can be accepted once more under AuthDigestNonceLifetime 0\n  or AuthDigestNcCheck; only stopping httpd (systemctl restart) invalidates\n  it (fixed upstream only in trunk f4c4160fbf, not in 2.4.69)\n- CVE-2026-63686: mod_xml2enc: avoid a NULL pointer dereference when a charset\n  conversion fails part way\n- CVE-2026-63045: mod_proxy_ftp: reject a PASV reply whose address differs from\n  the control connection peer\n- CVE-2026-42528: mod_dav: limit the number of shared locks on a resource\n- CVE-2026-93546: mod_dav_fs: cap the property database namespace table at 2048\n  entries\n- CVE-2026-58415: mod_dav_fs: deny access to the .DAV state directory for all\n  methods, including GET\n- CVE-2026-59797: mod_ssl: don't allow file() and filesize() in SSLRequire from\n  .htaccess files\n- CVE-2026-79768: mod_userdir: reject \".\" as a user name",
